### max_value

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"inl max_value () : date_time =\n    backend_switch {\n        Gleam = fun () =>\n            inl date : date_gleam = $'calendar.Date(9999, calendar.December, 31)' : date_gleam\n            inl time_of_day : time_of_day_gleam = $'calendar.TimeOfDay(23, 59, 59, 999)' : time_of_day_gleam\n            inl duration : duration_gleam = $'duration.seconds(0)  ' : duration_gleam\n            (date, time_of_day, duration) |> convert.to : date_time\n        Lua = fun () =>\n            inl date_time = $'os.time{year=9999, month=12, day=31, hour=23, min=59, sec=59} or 253402300799' : date_time\n            date_time\n        Fsharp = fun () => $'System.DateTime.MaxValue' : date_time\n        Python = fun () =>\n            global \"import datetime\"\n            $'datetime.datetime.max' : date_time\n        // .NET's MaxValue: the last 100 ns tick of 9999-12-31\n        Rust = fun () => $'chrono::NaiveDate::from_ymd_opt(9999, 12, 31).unwrap().and_hms_nano_opt(23, 59, 59, 999999900).unwrap()' : date_time\n    }","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  inl max_value () : date_time =
      backend_switch {
          Gleam = fun () =>
              inl date : date_gleam = $'calendar.Date(9999, calendar.December, 31)' : date_gleam
              inl time_of_day : time_of_day_gleam = $'calendar.TimeOfDay(23, 59, 59, 999)' : time_of_day_gleam
              inl duration : duration_gleam = $'duration.seconds(0)  ' : duration_gleam
              (date, time_of_day, duration) |> convert.to : date_time
          Lua = fun () =>
              inl date_time = $'os.time{year=9999, month=12, day=31, hour=23, min=59, sec=59} or 253402300799' : date_time
              date_time
          Fsharp = fun () => $'System.DateTime.MaxValue' : date_time
          Python = fun () =>
              global "import datetime"
              $'datetime.datetime.max' : date_time
          // .NET's MaxValue: the last 100 ns tick of 9999-12-31
          Rust = fun () => $'chrono::NaiveDate::from_ymd_opt(9999, 12, 31).unwrap().and_hms_nano_opt(23, 59, 59, 999999900).unwrap()' : date_time
      }
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

